  "articleBody": "Embarking on a remodeling project with a general contractor can be a fantastic experience, but it’s wise to be aware of common pitfalls so you can avoid them. One of the biggest mistakes is having an unclear scope from the start. Make sure your contract clearly defines every aspect of the project – what's included, what's not, and what the expectations are. A weak written contract can also lead to issues down the line, so ensure all agreements, especially around change orders, are in writing and well-understood by all parties. Speaking of change orders, poor control over them can quickly balloon your budget and timeline. Every change should be approved and documented. Another crucial step often overlooked is not verifying insurance and licensing. Always check that your contractor and their subcontractors are properly insured and licensed to protect yourself from liability. Lastly, always ask for and check references! This gives you insight into their communication style, reliability, and past project success. By sidestepping these common mistakes, you can set yourself up for a much smoother and more successful remodeling experience. Don't hesitate to seek professional advice if you're unsure about any of these steps; it can save you a lot of grief.",
